invariant: INV-26
file: ghash_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw GHASH data loop hashes whole blocks alone and drops a
  last partial block, so any associated data or ciphertext whose length is
  not a multiple of 16 authenticates without its last bytes, and a tag
  forged over different last bytes verifies. bin/ghash_equiv_test runs
  every data length through three passes against gcm.c's portable loop,
  which pads the last block, and every payload length through the whole
  AEAD. The edit is shared C after either instruction, so it lands on an
  ARMv8 runner and an x86-64 one alike.

--- old
    if (rest > 0) {
--- new
    if (rest > AES_BLOCK) {
